# Ruin-Lurker Bat: "At the beginning of YOUR end step, if you descended this turn, scry 1." Turn 2 Bot2's Lightning Bolt kills Bot1's Ornithopter, a permanent card
# going to Bot1's graveyard, so Bot1 descended on Bot2's turn (CR 700.11); the Bat does not trigger at Bot2's end step (it is not Bot1's end step) and
# the descent does not carry to Bot1's own end step on turn 3, where nothing went to the graveyard (the refusals; scenario "descended scries one" is the
# positive control that Arrange is asked when the condition holds).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Ruin-Lurker Bat
Ornithopter
Forest x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Lightning Bolt
Mountain
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ruin-Lurker Bat.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.End]
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Arrange
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
[T3 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Arrange

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Ruin-Lurker Bat.Power = 1
